# Map the historical author identities onto the repository owner.
#
# Every commit in this repository was authored as `ferhennn`, under two
# different addresses. GitHub resolves the noreply address
# ferhennn@users.noreply.github.com to an unrelated account, so anyone
# reading this history -- including integrations that derive deployment
# attribution from commit metadata, such as Vercel -- sees a stranger as the
# author instead of the person who owns the repository, and Vercel refuses the
# deployment with "not a member of this team".
#
# Rather than rewriting history (which would force-push 105 commits and
# invalidate every existing SHA), a mailmap re-attribution is declared here.
# It changes only how identities are *resolved* for display; the underlying
# commit objects and their hashes are untouched.

dev640 <83763869+dev640@users.noreply.github.com> ferhennn <ferhennn@users.noreply.github.com>
dev640 <83763869+dev640@users.noreply.github.com> ferhennn <sheikhfarhan2008@gmail.com>